name: the census
after: 18-xargs
intro: Four commands minimum from here. Build the pipeline one stage at a time
intro: and read the output of each before you add the next -- that is the actual
intro: skill, not memorising flags.
---
setup: Every ref file lists its flags on indented lines beginning with a dash.
setup: A character class avoids having to type a literal tab.
q: how many flags does /usr/share/learn/ref/ls document -- the number alone
a: grep -c '^[[:space:]]-' /usr/share/learn/ref/ls
a: grep -cE '^[[:space:]]+-' /usr/share/learn/ref/ls
ref: grep
cmp: ref
hint: -c counts matches instead of printing them
---
setup: In ls -l output the fifth field is the size in bytes.
q: total bytes under /usr/share/learn/ref, summing column 5 of ls -l with awk
a: ls -l /usr/share/learn/ref | awk '{s+=$5} END {print s}'
ref: awk
cmp: ref
hint: s+=$5 accumulates; END runs once, after every line has been seen
---
setup: Every level under /usr/share/learn/levels declares the commands it
setup: drills on ref: lines. Difference the whole corpus down to the unique set
setup: of commands the curriculum touches.
q: every command drilled in /usr/share/learn/levels, one per line, deduplicated
a: sed -n 's/^ref: //p' /usr/share/learn/levels/* | sort -u
a: grep -h '^ref: ' /usr/share/learn/levels/* | sed 's/^ref: //' | sort -u
why: live-hw
ref: sed
hint: strip the "ref: " prefix, then sort -u does the deduplicating
